---
permalink: /sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- sitemap.xml — every public page this build wrote, in every language.

   BUILT FROM collections.all, NOT FROM A LIST. src.11tydata.js turns a page
   off by refusing to write it at all, and its own comment gives the reason: a
   page that exists but is unlinked is "still crawlable, and still in the
   sitemap". Reading the collection keeps that promise — a page that was not
   built cannot appear here, and one that was cannot be forgotten. That covers
   the coming-soon collapse and the per-page toggles without naming either.

   ONE ENTRY PER TEMPLATE, EXPANDED TO FOUR URLS. The collection holds a single
   item per page — the first language pagination wrote — so the languages are
   expanded here with langSwap rather than read back out of the collection.
   Every public page is paginated over the same activeLangs, so what that
   produces is exactly what was built.

   ONLY THE PUBLIC PAGES. The collection also holds /admin/ and /staff/, which
   sit behind Cloudflare Access and have no business in a sitemap — and whose
   URLs carry no language segment, so asking langSwap for their translations
   produced four alternates all pointing back at themselves. The test is the
   first path segment: a page belongs here when it lives under a language this
   build published.

   Each URL then carries the whole group as alternates, itself included, which
   is the same set the page's own head declares — so the two cannot disagree. -#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
        xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
{%- for p in collections.all %}
{%- set seg = p.url.split("/")[1] if p.url else "" %}
{#- coming-soon is the landing page the site collapses TO. Under the dev server
   it is built at its own URL so it can be worked on, which is the only reason
   it is ever a page of its own — it is not somewhere to send a visitor. -#}
{%- if p.url and p.url.endsWith("/") and seg in activeLangs
       and "/coming-soon/" not in p.url %}
{%- for l in activeLangs %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ site.url }}{{ p.url | langSwap(l) }}</loc>
{%- for a in activeLangs %}
    <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="{{ a }}" href="{{ site.url }}{{ p.url | langSwap(a) }}"/>
{%- endfor %}
    <xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="{{ site.url }}{{ p.url | langSwap(site.defaultLang) }}"/>
  </url>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
